#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
ec2_inventory.py

Collects EC2 instance inventory across multiple AWS accounts (via cross-account
role assumption), builds a filterable/searchable HTML report with a client-side
CSV export button, and uploads the report to S3 under:

    s3://<bucket>/EC2Inventory/<Year>/<Month>/<Date>/<filename>.html
    s3://<bucket>/EC2Inventory/<Year>/<Month>/<Date>/<filename>.csv   (optional server-side copy)

Runs identically as:
  1. A CLI script:
       python3 ec2_inventory.py --bucket my-inventory-bucket
       python3 ec2_inventory.py --bucket my-inventory-bucket --regions us-east-1 ap-south-1
       python3 ec2_inventory.py --bucket my-inventory-bucket --regions ALL
       python3 ec2_inventory.py --no-upload --output-dir /tmp   # local file only

  2. An AWS Lambda function (handler = ec2_inventory.lambda_handler), configured via
     environment variables:
       BUCKET_NAME   (required)  - S3 bucket to upload the report to
       REGIONS       (optional)  - comma-separated regions, or "ALL". Defaults to DEFAULT_REGIONS below.
       EXTERNAL_ID   (optional)  - STS ExternalId used when assuming spoke roles

     Or by passing the same keys in the EventBridge/test event payload, e.g.:
       {"bucket": "my-inventory-bucket", "regions": "us-east-1,ap-south-1", "external_id": "..."}
     Event values take priority over environment variables.

Requires: boto3, botocore (already bundled in the standard AWS Lambda Python runtime;
          for CLI use: pip install boto3 --break-system-packages)
"""

